mhchem font extension for MathJax (@mathjax/mathjax-mhchem-font-extension 4.1.3)
==================================================================================

File: svg.js, copied unmodified from
https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@mathjax/mathjax-mhchem-font-extension@4.1.3/svg.js
(checked against the sha256 that jsDelivr publishes). The mhchem TeX
extension (\ce) loads it for its arrows and other chemistry glyphs.

Two licenses apply, as for the MathJax-Newcm font (../mathjax-newcm-font):

- The JavaScript packaging is by MathJax, Inc.; the package declares the
  Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE in this directory; the package ships no
  license file of its own).

- The glyph outline data is derived from the New Computer Modern fonts,
  (C) 2019-2021 Antonis Tsolomitis, released under the GUST Font License,
  i.e. the LaTeX Project Public License 1.3c or later. The package's own
  .woff2 file states this in its name table. The license texts are
  ../mathjax-newcm-font/GUST-FONT-LICENSE.txt and
  ../mathjax-newcm-font/LPPL-1.3c.txt.

  This is a modified version of New Computer Modern: MathJax converted the
  glyphs to SVG path data. It is redistributed here as MathJax published it,
  without further changes. The unmodified original fonts are available on
  CTAN as the package `newcomputermodern`
  (https://ctan.org/pkg/newcomputermodern). Redistributing it here implies
  no support from the original author; questions about this copy go to the
  ZiraDocs toolchain repository.
